    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="48.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 48.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="48.1" corresp="#wit-i">Ne nuls ne lait sun hum[e] de li partir pus que il est reté.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i">And no-one shall let any of his men leave him after an accusation has been brought against him.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="519"><ref target="clause:IICn_28-1">II Cn 28.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 28, 1</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 274–275 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
